WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.120
A recipe card, headed: revenge tragedy.

2
00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.910
The ingredients arrive.

3
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:06.990
A secret murder.

4
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.780
A ghost.

5
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:10.880
A clock, for delay.

6
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.500
A jester's cap, for madness.

7
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.130
A tiny stage on the stage.

8
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.970
A heap of swords.

9
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:23.870
Thomas Kyd set the pattern around 1587,
drawing on the Roman tragedian Seneca.

10
00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:29.160
Then, on an Elizabethan stage, a
figure picks up the card and hesitates.

11
00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.180
"The time is out of joint."

12
00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:35.000
So does Hamlet follow the
recipe, or rewrite it?

13
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.820
In this mission, you'll
trace the five-act shape,

14
00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.950
with the play scene at its centre.

15
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.750
And you'll listen to a
revenger who thinks aloud,

16
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.650
in seven soliloquies.

17
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.250
Your mission: decide whether Hamlet
follows the recipe or rewrites it.
